# fr04_edit_editor_vi_fallback.txtar — FR-4 / M2 acceptance: when neither
# $EDITOR nor $VISUAL is set, nesdit falls back to "vi".
#
# "vi" is registered as a no-op editor stub in main_test.go (via RunMain)
# so this fixture runs correctly regardless of whether the test machine has
# a real vi installed. The stub leaves the temp file unchanged (no
# FAKE_EDITOR_REPLACE set), so no change is detected and nesdit exits 0
# with "no change detected".
#
# This proves the resolution chain ($EDITOR → $VISUAL → "vi") reaches "vi"
# and that nesdit successfully invokes it.

env EDITOR=
env VISUAL=
env NESDIT_SKIP_TTY_CHECK=1

nesdit --edit input.yaml
stdout 'no change detected'

-- input.yaml --
replicas: 3
image: nginx
